\ Cross-check identical year candidates in native and signed-wide formats.
\ A six-gap year spanning 345 days is physically possible: each
\ canonical gate interval is at least 42 and at most 963 days.
\ All cases are synthetic; neither format invokes an expensive sauce.
\ Invalid candidates must remain invalid after widening.

The sample native year day is a calendar day.

To check the native and wide year candidate bridge:
  Put -15056000 into the first candidate's opening day.
  Put -15055655 into the first candidate's closing day.
  Put -5 into the first candidate's opening index.
  Put 1 into the first candidate's closing index.
  Measure the first candidate.
  If the first candidate's year length is not 345,
    put "Native year bridge fixture has the wrong duration." into the check report; exit.
  If the first candidate's span count is not 6,
    put "Native year bridge fixture has the wrong number of spans." into the check report; exit.
  Copy the first candidate into the first extended candidate.
  If the widened year conversion succeeded is not 1,
    put "A supported native year could not be widened." into the check report; exit.
  If the first extended candidate's valid is not 1,
    put "Widening a valid native year changed its eligibility." into the check report; exit.
  If the first extended candidate's year length is not "345",
    put "Widening a native year changed its day length." into the check report; exit.
  If the first extended candidate's span count is not "6",
    put "Widening a native year changed its gate span count." into the check report; exit.
  Put -15055671 into the sample native year day.
  Evaluate native year containment given the first candidate and the sample native year day.
  If the native year containment result is not 1,
    put "A valid native year excluded an interior day." into the check report; exit.
  Convert the sample native year day into the converted signed day result.
  Evaluate extended year containment given the first extended candidate and the converted signed day result.
  If the extended year containment result is not 1,
    put "A widened year excluded the same interior day." into the check report; exit.
  Put -15056000 into the sample native year day.
  Evaluate native year containment given the first candidate and the sample native year day.
  If the native year containment result is 1,
    put "The native year included the opening gate." into the check report; exit.
  Convert the sample native year day into the converted signed day result.
  Evaluate extended year containment given the first extended candidate and the converted signed day result.
  If the extended year containment result is 1,
    put "The widened year included the opening gate." into the check report; exit.
  Put -15055655 into the sample native year day.
  Evaluate native year containment given the first candidate and the sample native year day.
  If the native year containment result is not 1,
    put "The native year excluded the closing gate." into the check report; exit.
  Convert the sample native year day into the converted signed day result.
  Evaluate extended year containment given the first extended candidate and the converted signed day result.
  If the extended year containment result is not 1,
    put "The widened year excluded the closing gate." into the check report; exit.
  Put 0 into the first candidate's closing index.
  Measure the first candidate.
  Copy the first candidate into the first extended candidate.
  Evaluate native year containment given the first candidate and the sample native year day.
  If the native year containment result is 1,
    put "Native candidate with five gate spans was not rejected." into the check report; exit.
  If the first extended candidate's valid is not 0,
    put "Widened year with five gate spans was not rejected." into the check report; exit.
